GPU: the fixed function's near/far cull range from the viewport's MinZ and MaxZ

The XDK's lazy state setup (5659 0x304884) programs NV097_SET_CLIP_MIN / MAX as MinZ and MaxZ times the Z scale
for fixed function draws on untransformed vertices (0 to the Z scale for vertex programs and the W buffer), and
D3DRS_DEPTHCLIPCONTROL's D3DDCC_CULLPRIMITIVE culls outside it. The renderers culled every draw at 0 to the Z
scale. Counter-Strike's GL layer maps glDepthRange(0, 1) to MinZ -1 and MaxZ 1, so its screen fade (the
flashbang white-out), drawn by glOrtho at z 0, lands at depth -1: inside the console's range, outside ours.

FixedDepthCullRange gives the range; the reference renderer clips and culls with it (and clamps the depth to
the buffer's), the generated fixed function vertex shaders move z into it when DrawConstants::zcull is set so a
backend can take it back through the viewport's depth range.

